### Key ideas
- A transaction groups statements so they all succeed or all fail: `START TRANSACTION`, `COMMIT`, `ROLLBACK`, savepoints.
- Stored procedures are named, reusable blocks of SQL with parameters, called with `CALL`.

### Example
```sql
START TRANSACTION;
UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - 500 WHERE id = 1;
UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + 500 WHERE id = 2;
COMMIT;
```

